= Privacy Policy =
**Last updated:** 18 September 2026
**Effective from:** 18 September 2026
**Version:** 1.0

{{info}}
**Effective privacy notice.** This notice applies to the current static documentation site and its private aggregate page counter. It was checked against the repository and deployed data flow; it is not retained-counsel advice or sign-off.
{{/info}}

== At a glance ==

The Best Workplace is a public, static documentation site. It has no accounts, forms, payments, advertising, or user-submitted workplace data.

When a page opens, GitHub serves the site; Google Fonts and cdnjs/Cloudflare serve fonts and Mermaid code; embedded remote images may contact their source. The site sends the internal page reference, prefixed with the BestWorkplace site ID, to a Cloudflare Worker that increments an aggregate page-view total. It sends no visitor identifier and creates no analytics cookie or local-storage identifier. Cloudflare receives the visitor's IP address and ordinary request metadata at the network layer, but the project Worker does not write those data to Workers KV. Page totals are visible only through the operator's authenticated Cloudflare account.

== 1. Controller and contact ==

The site's content is maintained and privately operated by **Robert Schaub**:

* **Controller:** Robert Schaub (private project operator)
* **Postal address:** In Lederäcker 11, 8305 Dietlikon, Switzerland
* **Privacy requests:** in writing to the postal address above

GitHub, Google, Cloudflare/cdnjs, and remote media hosts determine some processing independently for their services.

== 2. Scope ==

This notice covers the public BestWorkplace GitHub Pages site, the public GitHub repository, its documentation analytics Worker, and direct project communications. It does not cover external sites reached by selecting a link.

== 3. Data, purposes, and recipients ==

|= Activity |= Data and recipient |= Purpose |
| Visit a page | GitHub receives IP address and ordinary HTTP metadata; GitHub states that Pages visitor IP addresses are logged for security | Deliver and secure the static site |
| Render fonts and diagrams | Google Fonts and cdnjs/Cloudflare receive ordinary request metadata such as IP address and user agent | Render typography and Mermaid diagrams |
| Load embedded remote media | The image or media host receives an ordinary request when embedded content loads | Display referenced material |
| Aggregate page-view count | The internal page reference, prefixed with `BW`, is sent to a Cloudflare Worker. Cloudflare receives the IP address and ordinary request metadata at the network layer; Workers KV stores only the total count for each page. | Understand which public documentation pages are used |
| Contribute on GitHub | GitHub identity, contribution, timestamp, commit/review metadata | Public review, attribution, correction, and project history |
| Contact the maintainer | Email address, message, attachments, correspondence metadata | Reply and handle the request |

The counter payload does not include your name, email address, page text, IP address, browser fingerprint, or another visitor identifier. The Worker accepts browser writes only from the configured GitHub Pages origin and only for the configured BestWorkplace site ID. There is no public statistics endpoint. Counts remain approximate operational indicators rather than audited measurements.

== 4. Browser storage and historical minimisation ==

The page-view counter does not use cookies, `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, or another browser identifier. The viewer removes the retired `fh_vid` value on a return visit if an older deployment left it in this browser.

The earlier Worker stored per-page counters by random browser UUID in the same namespace for FactHarbor and BestWorkplace. On 18 September 2026 those UUID maps were removed from the existing records while the aggregate page-view totals were preserved. The retained totals no longer permit cross-project linkage through the former identifier.

The shared `https://robertschaub.github.io` origin also serves FactHarbor and Our AI Charter. Neither site currently sends a visitor identifier to this Worker.

== 5. Legal grounds and international transfers ==

Processing follows the Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection principles of lawfulness, good faith, transparency, purpose limitation, proportionality, accuracy, and security. Where the GDPR applies, site delivery, security, project maintenance, and correspondence may rely on legitimate interests (Article 6(1)(f)), requested project steps (Article 6(1)(b)), or legal obligations (Article 6(1)(c)).

The private operator uses the aggregate page totals to understand use of the public documentation. Where the GDPR applies, the intended basis is the operator's legitimate interest in maintaining and prioritising that documentation, subject to the absence of a visitor identifier and to the user's overriding rights. Ordinary site use is not treated as blanket consent for additional tracking.

GitHub, Google, and Cloudflare may process data outside Switzerland. GitHub, Google Fonts, cdnjs/Cloudflare and remote-media hosts determine ordinary website-delivery, security and service-log processing independently under their own terms. Cloudflare processes the Worker's page reference and aggregate KV totals on the controller's instructions under its customer data-processing addendum; Cloudflare separately determines processing of its account, network-security and service data.

For transfers to the United States, the controller relies on a current Swiss–US Data Privacy Framework certification where it covers the relevant recipient and service, or on recognised Standard Contractual Clauses with the required Swiss adaptations. Cloudflare's customer DPA expressly provides for the EU SCCs as adapted to the Swiss FADP where required. Other independent providers apply their own published transfer safeguards; the controller limits its own counter payload to the project/page reference and does not send a visitor identifier.

Provider notices:

* [[GitHub General Privacy Statement>>https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement]]
* [[Google Privacy Policy>>https://policies.google.com/privacy]]
* [[Cloudflare Privacy Policy>>https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/]]
* [[Cloudflare Customer Data Processing Addendum>>https://www.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-customer-dpa/]]

== 6. Retention ==

|= Data |= Retention period / criterion |
| Aggregate page-view totals in Workers KV | Retained while useful for maintaining the public documentation and reviewed at least annually. They contain no visitor identifier. The operator resets or deletes totals that are no longer needed through the authenticated Cloudflare account. |
| GitHub Pages, Google Fonts, cdnjs/Cloudflare, and remote-media logs | Set by the respective provider; not directly deletable by this site's controller |
| Public GitHub contributions and history | Retained as a durable public record and may remain in forks, clones, releases, or archives |
| Direct correspondence | Up to two years after closure unless law, an active dispute, or a documented security need requires longer; reviewed at least annually |

We do not sell personal data or use page-view totals for advertising or individual profiling.

== 7. Rights and security ==

Depending on applicable law and circumstances, you may request access, correction, deletion, restriction, objection, or data release/portability by writing to the controller address in §1. We may verify identity or authority before disclosing or changing data.

Public Git history cannot always be fully erased from distributed copies. We will nevertheless assess reasonable correction, redaction, deletion, or platform measures. You may complain to the [[Swiss Federal Data Protection and Information Commissioner (FDPIC)>>https://www.edoeb.admin.ch/en]] or, where the GDPR applies, the competent EU/EEA supervisory authority.

The site uses HTTPS through GitHub Pages and public source code, but no internet service can guarantee absolute security. Do not place secrets, private correspondence, or unnecessary personal data in public issues or contributions.

== 8. Children and changes ==

The site is general workplace-learning material and is not designed to collect children's data. Do not submit personal data about a child in a public contribution.

Material changes will be versioned in the repository and state their effective date. This notice is reviewed before new forms, embeds, visitor identifiers, public statistics, or materially different analytics are enabled.

== 9. Operating decisions and review triggers ==

1. Remote Google Fonts, cdnjs/Mermaid and embedded images remain enabled because they are part of the current public documentation presentation; their requests and independent provider processing are disclosed above.
2. Statistics remain private to the operator. There is no public statistics endpoint or visible visitor counter.
3. Rights requests are handled in writing at the address in §1; identity or authority is verified where needed, and the operator targets an initial response within 30 days.
4. The operator reviews aggregate totals and correspondence at least annually and deletes them when the retention criterion above is no longer met.
5. The notice and necessity of external assets are re-audited before a new form, visitor identifier, public statistic, repository macro or materially different analytics is enabled.
